    },
    {
      "paper_id": "doi-10-1038-s41598-025-32765-6",
      "decision": "ADMIT",
      "reason": "The abstract targets the exact binary identity question of whether mentions denote the same real-world occurrence and uses causal intervention plus counterfactual trigger perturbation to separate superficial lexical matching from evidence supplied by event arguments. This is directly useful for the open question of what evidence actually supports or refutes continuity and for guarding against false merges caused by surface similarity. Identifier is UNCHECKED, but the contribution is distinct from the verified candidates.",
