    },
    {
      "paper_id": "doi-10-3115-1220575-1220591",
      "decision": "ADMIT",
      "reason": "The abstract explicitly separates similarity based on names, topics, and full text for new-event detection. This is valuable transfer evidence for the project's central distinction that shared entities or topic similarity can contribute to continuity decisions without defining identity by themselves, and it provides a cleaner evidence-factorization angle than generic new-event detection papers. Identifier is UNCHECKED.",
