    {
      "paper_id": "doi-10-1016-j-lingua-2011-02-004",
      "decision": "REJECT",
      "reason": "The continuum from identity through near-identity to non-identity is conceptually relevant, but the abstract is general coreference semantics rather than event-specific or workplace identity. The admitted subevent paper provides much more direct evidence for the concrete partial-event distinction needed here, so this broader linguistic treatment does not justify an additional reading slot. Identifier is UNCHECKED."
    },
    {
      "paper_id": "doi-10-18653-v1-2023-emnlp-main-294",
      "decision": "ADMIT",
      "reason": "The abstract directly evaluates cross-document same-event clustering and adds document-level rhetorical structure plus dependency-path evidence beyond local mention features. This materially strengthens F1 because it tests whether structural/contextual evidence contributes to identity judgments, an important analogue for the project's need to combine content with source and discourse relationships without equating those relationships with identity. Identifier is UNCHECKED.",
