      "decision": "REJECT",
      "reason": "The paper is clearly in F1, but the abstract emphasizes X-AMR representation, multi-hop linearization of pairwise decisions, and assessment of LLM judgments. It does not show a distinctive analysis of identity evidence or partial/evolving relations, and its contribution is more about representation and computational organization than the current open gaps. Stronger verified and unverified F1 candidates are admitted."
    },
    {
      "paper_id": "2406.02148",
      "decision": "REJECT",
      "reason": "The abstract demonstrates another capable cross-document event-coreference architecture, but its main contribution is LLM-assisted event understanding and representation learning. It does not expose which evidence establishes or refutes identity, how uncertainty is handled, or how partial identity is distinguished, so it adds little to the specific gaps relative to the admitted F1 papers."
    },
    {
      "paper_id": "manual-17ac9fedf9",
      "decision": "REJECT",
      "reason": "Creating coherent cross-document context is relevant, but this capability substantially overlaps the admitted discourse/context paper and the separate 2025 coherence-and-structure candidate. The abstract does not show a unique evidence analysis, work-domain result, or identity-relation distinction sufficient to justify another slot. Identifier is UNCHECKED."
    },
